### Test GET Orders API - Secure Endpoint
### This file tests the GET /api/v1/orders endpoint with authentication

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@apiKey = pk_your_api_key_here
@vendorCode = YOUR_VENDOR_CODE_HERE

### 1. Test without authorization (should fail with 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?vendorCode={{vendorCode}}

###

### 2. Test with invalid API key format (should fail with 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?vendorCode={{vendorCode}}
Authorization: Bearer invalid_key

###

### 3. Test without vendor code (should fail with 400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###

### 4. Test with valid API key and vendor code (should succeed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?vendorCode={{vendorCode}}
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###

### 5. Test with pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?vendorCode={{vendorCode}}&limit=10&offset=0
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###

### 6. Test with wrong vendor code (should fail with 401 or 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?vendorCode=WRONG123
Authorization: Bearer {{apiKey}}

###

### 7. Test with another vendor's API key (should fail with 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders?vendorCode={{vendorCode}}
Authorization: Bearer pk_another_vendors_api_key_here

###

